// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/widgets/lut-treemap.t27 -- which submodule eats my LUTs: a treemap from yosys `stat -json`
; Source of truth for public/widgets/lut-treemap/ (gHashTag/trinity, apps/website). The page is
; written by scripts/widget-pages-from-spec.mjs from this file; tool.js holds no English of its
; own and reads every word below from window.T27_WIDGET.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT IT DOES: the reader drops the JSON that yosys `stat -json` wrote for a design that was NOT
; flattened. In that JSON every module lists its own cells by type and, under the same map, how
; many instances of each submodule it holds. public/widgets/lut-treemap/treemap.js multiplies down
; the hierarchy: a module's instance count is the sum, over every path from the top, of the
; product of the counts on that path; its share is instances x its own cells. The page draws one
; tile per instance (or one tile marked xN when there are too many), sized by LUTs, FFs, DSPs or
; BRAMs, with a table of every module: instances, cells of one, total, share. It checks that the
; tiles add up to the top's total and to the total yosys printed itself. A second, optional drop
; takes the stat of a flattened run of the same design and shows both totals side by side. Files
; are read in the browser and never leave the page; nothing is sent.

; THE SAMPLE: gf16_matmul4x4_p, a pipelined 4x4 matrix multiplier over GF16 (16 gf16_dot4_p, each
; 3 gf16_add and 4 gf16_mul). Two of its files are in gHashTag/trinity, fpga/gf16-pipelined/, and
; the combinational gf16_add and gf16_mul with ports a, b, result are in gHashTag/t27,
; fpga/vivado/. scripts/widget-data/lut-treemap.mjs reads the four files out of git at the commits
; named below, copies them to a scratch directory and runs Yosys 0.67+post twice: synth_xilinx
; -top gf16_matmul4x4_p, and the same with -flatten, each followed by `tee -q -o <file> stat
; -json`. Both outputs are shipped byte for byte; sample.json holds the commands, the `yosys -V`
; line, exit codes, seconds and the sha256 of every input. Every K_SAMPLE_ fact below is re-read
; from those files by `node scripts/widget-data/lut-treemap.mjs --check`, which also runs this
; spec's tests on the values it read and a negative control that must fail them.

; WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: these are synthesis cell counts, not post-place-and-route utilisation.
; A hierarchical run keeps module boundaries, so yosys cannot optimise across them: the sample's
; flattened run comes out at 18730 LUT against 20464 hierarchical. The per-module split is true of
; the hierarchical build only, and the page says so whenever both totals are shown. stat -json
; names no instances, so the copies of a module are numbered in counting order, not by instance
; name. The cell lists are 7-series names (synth_xilinx, the default family); other cells are
; counted under "other" and are not drawn.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

